-## Update: the crystal ball, the unicorn sword, crystals, mushrooms, crawfish, shell armor and the Dragon
-
-(Where this contradicts an earlier section, this one holds.)
-
-- **Newts** are drawn and hit-boxed twice their old size (`NEWT_MODEL_SCALE`, `NEWT_HALF_WIDTH` 0.5, `NEWT_HEIGHT` 0.36). Each always drops `NEWT_EYE_DROP_MIN..=MAX` (1 to 2) Eyes of Newt; an eye is food (`NEWT_EYE_HEAL` 1, through `ItemKind::heal_amount`).
-- **Crystal Ball** (`ItemKind::CrystalBall`): `CRYSTAL_BALL_STARDUST` (10) Stardust (the only "dust" item) craft one. A left click with it held (`Game::attack` -> `Game::use_crystal_ball`) calls `set_night(!night)`; it does nothing during a blackout or in the Horizen (always day). It breaks no blocks (`Block::can_break_with`). `Game::apply_night` counts every real switch in `Game::day_night_switches` (stews count too), saved as `switches <n>`.
-- **Unicorn Horn / Sword**: the Unicorn also drops `UNICORN_HORN_DROP` horn; Horn + Leather Cord craft a `UnicornSword` (`UNICORN_SWORD_DAMAGE` = Excalibur + 8, same cooldown and reach). Only Excalibur gets `EXCALIBUR_HUNT_FACTOR`.
-- **Vampire Bat**: model scale `VAMPIRE_BAT_MODEL_SCALE` 2.8 (was 3.4), `VAMPIRE_BAT_HALF_WIDTH` 0.6. Outside its dive `Animal::centre_in_passage` draws its goal height towards the middle between floor and ceiling (at least `VAMPIRE_BAT_CEILING_MARGIN` under the roof), takes out the part of the goal that lies into a nearby wall (`VAMPIRE_BAT_WALL_NEAR`) and adds a sideways push (`VAMPIRE_BAT_CENTRE_SPEED`) towards the more open side.
-- **Crystals**: `Block::RedCrystal` is gone; crystal caves hold `RubyCrystal`, `SapphireCrystal` and `AmethystCrystal` (`horizen::crystal_block`), solid, hand-breakable (`BREAK_SECONDS_CRYSTAL`), dropping `CRYSTAL_DROP_MIN..=MAX` of `ItemKind::Ruby`/`Sapphire`/`Amethyst`. Removals are saved like any generated block. A sling (`Game::shoot`) uses a crystal first (ruby, sapphire, amethyst), then pebbles; `Arrow::damage` is `SLING_DAMAGE * CRYSTAL_DAMAGE_FACTOR` (4) for them, and a miss lands as the crystal item.
-- **Mushroom caves** (`horizen::CaveKind::Mushroom`, `mushroom_at`): `HORIZEN_MUSHROOM_PERCENT` of the ordinary caves, taken from the *plain* band of the cave-kind roll so older worlds keep their mossy/river/crystal caves. `Block::Mushroom` is walk-through and hand-breakable and drops `ItemKind::Mushroom`. Eating one (`Game::eat_held`) costs `MUSHROOM_DAMAGE` and sets `Game::speed_boost` to `MUSHROOM_BOOST_SECONDS`; `apply_worn_effects` multiplies `Player::speed_factor` by `MUSHROOM_SPEED_FACTOR` while it lasts (`Game::update_effects` counts it down).
-- **Crawfish** (`AnimalKind::Crawfish`, `BigCrawfish`, `GiantCrawfish`, `AnimalKind::is_aquatic`): they only move onto wet columns (the `is_aquatic` branch of `Animal::update`), placed by `Game::spawn_aquatic`. Small ones (`spawn_crawfish`, normal-world water) are harmless, 4 health, one in five drops a `ShellFragment`. Big ones (`spawn_big_crawfish`, `horizen::river_at` in river caves) have 20 health, ignore the player until hurt (`Animal::enraged`) and then strike, and always drop 1-2 fragments. `Game::note_big_crawfish_killed` counts kills (`crawfishkills <n>`); every `BIG_CRAWFISH_KILLS_PER_GIANT` makes one Giant Crawfish due (`giant_crawfish_owed`, `summon_giant_crawfish`: 120 health, boss, never gives up, 10-20 fragments; one left behind in another dimension is due again).
-- **Shell Armor**: `SHELL_ARMOR_FRAGMENTS` (50) fragments craft it; it is a worn item. `Game::hurt_player` takes `SHELL_ARMOR_REDUCTION` off each blow but never more than half (rounded up).
-- **The Dragon** (`AnimalKind::Dragon`, boss, `flies_always`, `never_gives_up`): `Game::spawn_bosses` brings one to the Skylands (`DRAGON_SPAWN_DISTANCE` away, `DRAGON_SPAWN_HEIGHT` up) whenever `day_night_switches >= DRAGON_SWITCHES` and none is out; killing it sets the count back to 0 (`boss_slain`). `Animal::update_flier`: it circles high up, hangs in the air to breathe (`BossAction::Breathe`, one `BossEvent::DragonFlame` every `DRAGON_BREATH_SECONDS / DRAGON_BREATH_FLAMES`, which `carry_out` turns into a jittered `ProjectileKind::DragonFire`), and swoops (`AirPhase::Dive`); its strike throws the player `AnimalKind::strike_knockback` blocks (`Player::launch`). Its hit box (`DRAGON_HIT_HALF_WIDTH`) is wider than its collision box. Model: `animal_draw::dragon_parts`. Drops `DRAGON_GOLD_DROP` gold.
-- Save format additions: `switches <n>`, `crawfishkills <n>`; item ids `ruby`, `sapphire`, `amethyst`, `mushroom`, `crystal_ball`, `unicorn_horn`, `unicorn_sword`, `shell_fragment`, `shell_armor`.
