-## Update: the jungle floor, fairies, goats, moonlight, ivory knives and quail drops
-
-(Where this contradicts an earlier section, this one holds.)
-
-- **Yeti smash**: `YETI_SMASH_RADIUS` is 6 (three times the old 2) and `YETI_SMASH_TRIGGER_RANGE` is 6, so it rears up whenever the player is inside what it can reach (beyond `YETI_ICE_MIN_RANGE`, which is the same number, it throws ice).
-- **Falling stars** come every `FALLING_STAR_INTERVAL` 5 seconds (twice as often).
-- **Jungle ponds** (`terrain::jungle_pond`, `jungle_pond_site`, used by `terrain::surface`): on a grid of `JUNGLE_POND_CELL` squares, `JUNGLE_POND_PERCENT` hold a small wavy pond, cut one block into flat ground like a river (so `is_wet_column`, wading, crawfish and the jar all work). None within `JUNGLE_POND_CLEARING_MARGIN` of the bare middle, on a hill, or beside a valley. **Darker grass**: `mesh.rs` paints the jungle's ground top `JUNGLE_GRASS_COLOR`.
-- **Foliage** (`Block::Foliage`, `Block::FigFoliage`, generated in `terrain::generate_chunk_for` on `JUNGLE_FOLIAGE_PERCENT` of dry jungle columns outside the bare middle, one clump in `JUNGLE_FIG_ONE_IN` with figs): walk-through, hand-breakable (`BREAK_SECONDS_GROUND_FOLIAGE`, `BREAK_SECONDS_FIG_FOLIAGE`). Plain foliage drops nothing. `Block::is_pickable` (bush and fig foliage): right click harvests once (`World::berry_picked`, saved, fruit not drawn) and `Game::pick_berry_bush` gives `FIG_PICK_MIN..=MAX` figs; breaking fig foliage gives `FIG_BREAK_MIN..=MAX`. `ItemKind::Fig` heals `FIG_HEAL` 3.
-- **Moonlight** (`ItemKind::MoonlightVial`, `Game::moonlight`, `max_health`, `drink_moonlight`): right click drinks. Each vial adds one extra heart (new heart full) up to `MOONLIGHT_MAX_BONUS` 10 and sets every timer in `Game::moonlight` back to `MOONLIGHT_SECONDS` 60; `update_effects` counts them down and drops expired hearts (health is clamped). Healing caps at `max_health()`. Dying clears them. Not saved (`serialize_save_full` writes at most `MAX_HEALTH`). `play::draw_health` draws a second row, in blue, past ten.
-- **Fairies** (`AnimalKind::Fairy`, `Animal::update_fairy`, `Game::spawn_sky_wildlife`, `spawn_sky_creature`): Skylands only, hovering `FAIRY_HOVER_HEIGHT` over an island, `FAIRY_HEALTH` 8, no damage. Every `FAIRY_PLANT_MIN..=MAX` seconds (`Animal::special_timer`) an unroused fairy plants a `Block::Flower` on the grass below it (`Game::update_fairy_planting`; `Block::Flower` is in `PLAYER_MADE`, id `flower`, so it is saved as a placed block). A blow on any fairy (`Game::hurt_animals_from`) sets `enraged` on all; roused fairies fly to the side of the player away from the nearest edge (`Animal::edge_direction`, `FAIRY_EDGE_SEARCH`), and `try_attack` pushes (`strike_knockback` `FAIRY_KNOCKBACK`, via `Player::launch`) every `FAIRY_ATTACK_COOLDOWN`. They calm when the player dies or is `FAIRY_GIVE_UP_DISTANCE` away. **Trade**: `Game::trade_with_fairy` (right click, ash held, fairy within `FAIRY_TRADE_REACH`, from `play::handle_placing`) swaps one Ash for a Vial of Moonlight; a roused fairy refuses. The general store's ghost says `ghosts::SHOP_ASH_HINT` instead of his greeting when the inventory holds ash.
-- **Mountain goats** (`AnimalKind::MountainGoat`): Skylands islands, `GOAT_HEALTH` 30, ignore the player until hit (`enraged`, like the moose), then charge at `GOAT_RUN_SPEED` for `GOAT_DAMAGE` 1 with `GOAT_KNOCKBACK` blocks of throw. They turn from (wandering) or stop at (charging) the edge of an island. They drop `GOAT_HORN_DROP` Goat Horn; 1 horn crafts `IVORY_KNIVES_PER_HORN` Ivory Knives. Fairies and goats that fall below `SKY_VOID_Y` are removed.
-- **Ivory Knife** (`ItemKind::IvoryKnife`, `ItemKind::is_thrown`, `Game::throw_knife`, `Arrow::thrown_knife`): thrown like an iron feather (`IVORY_KNIFE_DAMAGE`, `IVORY_KNIFE_THROW_COOLDOWN`), but `Game::update_arrows` drops it where it hits an animal as well as where it lands: it is never used up.
-- **Iron Quails** no longer drop a Silver Key: `IRON_QUAIL_IRON_DROP` iron and `IRON_QUAIL_IRON_FEATHER_DROP` iron feathers. **Bronze Parrots** drop `BRONZE_PARROT_BRONZE_DROP` bronze and `BRONZE_PARROT_IRON_FEATHER_DROP` iron feathers. Silver keys come from the mines' key stands and the graveyard ghost (`Game::key_or_gold` still applies).
-- Save format additions: item ids `fig`, `moonlight_vial`, `goat_horn`, `ivory_knife`; placed block id `flower`.
+- An arrow that hits a plant-covered cell is not stopped by the plant.
+- Rivers are one block deep: you wade through them; there is no swimming.
+- Dying respawns the player at the spawn point, which may be where a bear is waiting. This holds with the King's Crown too.
+- The ruined castle, the lake and the others have no ghostly lead except the ones described above (the crown does not show a trail).
+- The sites are hundreds of blocks away: tests reach them by teleporting and streaming chunks, which is slow for big loops.
